// =============================================================================
// investing-course — "How Investing Actually Works: Risk, Time, and the
// Steward's Question"
// =============================================================================
// Course FOUR of the Stock Market department, and the last quarter of the
// sentence Darrell spoke on 2026-09-19: "Stock Market courses to explore and
// explain the world of stock and bonds and countries that trade and how
// investment works world wide." Course one answered STOCK, course two BONDS,
// course three COUNTRIES THAT TRADE. This one answers HOW INVESTMENT WORKS.
//
// WHY THIS IS THE HARDEST COURSE IN THE DEPARTMENT TO WRITE HONESTLY. The
// first three teach MACHINERY: what a share is, what a bond is, what a deficit
// is. A reader can be handed those and be strictly better off. This one is
// about a DECISION -- and a decision is exactly where teaching turns into
// telling somebody what to do with their money without anybody noticing the
// step. The whole course is built so that every lesson ends by handing the
// reader a QUESTION to take to their own situation rather than an answer this
// house supplies. Nothing here names a product, a fund, an allocation, or a
// "most people should". That is not caution; it is the subject matter. A
// person who finishes this course should be harder to sell to, including by us.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. What investing actually is -- deferring use      (Proverbs 13:11)
//   2. Risk is four different things wearing one word   (Genesis 41:35, 36)
//   3. Time is the only free ingredient                 (Proverbs 21:5)
//   4. Spreading it out -- and what that cannot do      (Ecclesiastes 11:2)
//   5. Cost is the one number known in advance          (Proverbs 27:23)
//   6. What cannot be known, and who sells certainty    (James 4:13, 14)
//   7. The steward's question                           (Luke 16:11)
//   8. Enough                                           (Proverbs 30:8)
//
// THE FOUR RISKS, because flattening them is the commonest failure in this
// subject. "Risky" is used for all four and they behave completely
// differently: (a) the money does not come back at all; (b) the money is
// there but you cannot reach it when you need it; (c) the money is there and
// reachable and buys less than it did; (d) you are forced to sell at the worst
// possible moment by something that has nothing to do with the investment.
// Lesson two separates them and every later lesson keeps them separate.
//
// THE LINE ON COMPOUNDING (DR-0076 sec.4, measure don't claim). The arithmetic
// in lesson three is DONE in the lesson, with its assumption written on its
// face and labelled as an assumption, never presented as a forecast and never
// attached to a real instrument. An illustration that shows what a rate does
// over a period is arithmetic. The same illustration with a real fund's name
// beside it is a sales document, and this course never crosses that line.
//
// THE LINE ON SPREADING IT OUT (lesson four). Ecclesiastes 11:2 gives the
// practice AND its limit in the same verse -- "Give a portion to seven, and
// also to eight" is the practice, "for thou knowest not what evil shall be
// upon the earth" is the reason, and the reason is an admission of ignorance
// rather than a promise of safety. Spreading reduces the harm from ONE thing
// failing. It does nothing about everything falling together, and a course
// that implies otherwise has sold comfort under the name of teaching.
//
// AND WHAT THIS COURSE REFUSES TO DO. It gives no financial advice, names no
// product, fund, company, platform or strategy, quotes no live figure, and
// makes no forecast. Where a reader's real decision is involved it says so and
// points them to somebody who can look at their actual situation.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). Every quoted span is
// fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV. Our prose says Yahweh;
// quotations keep "God" and "the LORD" exactly as the KJV has them (DR-0210).
//
// TEACHING, NOT FINANCIAL ADVICE -- carried on the meta.
// =============================================================================

