        body: 'A father asked his daughter to explain what was risky about the money she had put aside, and she said it might go down. He asked her to write four columns instead and fill each one in. She got through the first two quickly and stalled on the fourth, which asked what in her own life could force her to sell. She sat with it and then wrote one word: the van. The van was eleven years old and she used it for work. Nothing about the investment had changed in the ten minutes it took to write that word, and she understood it completely differently afterwards.',
