        body: 'A teacher stopped explaining compounding to her class because she noticed they were nodding rather than understanding. She handed out calculators and made every one of them do thirty rounds by hand, which took most of the lesson and produced a certain amount of complaining. The room went quiet somewhere around round twenty-two. Afterwards one of them said he had heard the word his whole life and had thought it meant money grows, and that it had never once occurred to him that the same rate gives you seven at the start and fifty at the end.',
