    lesson: 'EVERY OTHER INGREDIENT IN THIS SUBJECT IS PURCHASABLE. Counsel can be bought, access can be bought, information and tools and the services of people much cleverer than you can all be bought. TIME CANNOT BE BOUGHT BY ANYONE AT ANY PRICE. A person beginning at twenty-two holds something a person beginning at forty-two cannot obtain by any means whatever, and it is the largest single advantage anywhere in this business. It is also the most consistently wasted, because it arrives free, without ceremony, and does nothing visible for a decade. THE ARITHMETIC, DONE RATHER THAN ASSERTED, WITH ITS ASSUMPTION ON ITS FACE. Begin with 100. Apply a factor of 1.07 — SEVEN PER CENT IS AN ASSUMPTION CHOSEN TO MAKE THE ILLUSTRATION LEGIBLE, not a projection, not a promise, and not a claim about any real thing that exists. One application gives 107. Two gives about 114.5. Three, about 122.5. Four, about 131.1. After ten applications the sum stands at about 197, very nearly doubled. After twenty, about 387. After thirty, about 761. NOW EXAMINE WHERE THE INCREASE ACTUALLY HAPPENS, because this is what turns a familiar fact into a usable one. THE FIRST APPLICATION ADDS EXACTLY 7.00. THE THIRTIETH ADDS ABOUT 49.80 — ABOUT SEVEN TIMES AS MUCH, FROM AN IDENTICAL RATE. The rate never changed by a hair. What changed is the quantity the rate was working on, and the only way to have more of that quantity is to have started earlier. THE CONSEQUENCE IS NOT INTUITIVE AND IS WORTH SAYING DIRECTLY. The first ten applications feel like nothing, produce almost nothing visible, and are the applications that make the final ten possible. That is exactly why people abandon the exercise during them and afterwards report that the whole thing does not work. IT DOES WORK. It simply does its conspicuous work at the end, out of material that had to be supplied at the beginning — WHICH MEANS THE MOST VALUABLE ACTION IN THIS ENTIRE SUBJECT IS ALSO THE DULLEST: beginning, with a modest sum, and then not interfering. TWO HONEST QUALIFICATIONS, because this is the most abused illustration in the field. FIRST, 1.07 was chosen for clarity. Nothing promises anybody seven per cent, real holdings do not advance in a smooth line, and some stretches go backwards for several years together — a person who has only ever seen the smooth curve is unprepared for the actual experience of holding the thing, and being unprepared for it is how people end up selling during the part that was always going to happen. SECOND, AND THIS IS THE BRIGHT LINE OF THE WHOLE COURSE: an illustration of what a rate does across a period is ARITHMETIC. The identical illustration with the name of something purchasable printed beside it is a SALES DOCUMENT. The distance between the two is one line of type, it is crossed constantly, and it is very often crossed deliberately by people who will tell you afterwards that they were only educating. This house shows the arithmetic and does not print the name. Scripture names the temperament the arithmetic requires and names its opposite in the same breath: "The thoughts of the diligent tend only to plenteousness; but of every one that is hasty only to want." (Proverbs 21:5) DILIGENCE HERE IS NOT FRANTIC EXERTION. It is the settled continuing kind — thoughts that TEND, holding a direction across a long interval. And HASTE IS NOT SPEED; a diligent person may work extremely fast. HASTE IS THE WISH TO ARRIVE WITHOUT GOING THROUGH THE INTERVAL. The verse says where each one ends up, and the thirty lines of arithmetic above are that verse with numbers attached to it.',
